  "id": "body-size-overestimation",
  "term": "body-size overestimation",
  "definition": "Body-size overestimation is a form of body image distortion in which a person perceives their body as larger than it actually is. In this study, it was expressed as a perceived body size or BMI that was higher than the person’s real body size or BMI.",
